// The owner's words (tickets-patterns semantics.tex, The owner's words; rule File). No longer opened: the owner's
// message opens a thread (thread.kind); old filings replay as recorded. Each thing the owner types opens
// a filing, with no opener; the clerk splits it into pieces, each a span of the text with the ticket it belongs on.
// When the filing closes, the rule File posts each piece on its ticket as the owner's (or answers the owner's step
// with it, where the piece names the result). What cannot be placed fails the filing, and the owner is told.
//
// An agent's turn is no longer filed (paper-research m952): the rule Reply posts a turn given one post as its reply,
// in the machine. A filing in an old log with `by` (an agent's turn) is no longer filed when replayed.
/// the owner's words split by the clerk into pieces, each posted on its ticket; no longer opened
kind filing
  letter F
  form text: Text
  result Filed(pieces: [Piece])
  raises Unplaced
  pattern
    f <- step clerk file(text);
    match f {
      Filed(pieces) => return Filed(pieces)
      Unplaced(why, left) => raise Unplaced(why)
    }
